---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EDGES, FACULTY, inquiryLink } from '../../data/program';

const title = 'Bring It In-House: The Enterprise Edge';
const description =
  'Run The Enterprise Edge for your own revenue team, or as the anchor session at your sales kickoff. Half day, three edges, built around the deals your team is actually working. For organizations with 50+ sellers.';
const canonical = 'https://getenterpriseedge.com/in-house/';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>

  <section class="band band-ink hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">In-house and sales kickoffs</p>
      <h1>Run it for your own team, with your own deals on the table.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The public sessions use examples. An in-house session uses yours: the stalled deal, the account that will not expand, the price challenge you lost last quarter.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-bone band-measure">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What changes</p>
      <h2>Same three edges. A very different room.</h2>
      <p>In a public session, a room of strangers compares notes. In-house, everyone owns a piece of the same number, which means the conversation can get specific in a way a public room never can.</p>
      <p>We work your pipeline. Your champion, your buying group, your last three losses. By the end of the half day the team has one story to align on and a shared read on where deals are leaking.</p>
      <p>At a sales kickoff it runs as the anchor session, three hours that give the rest of the agenda something to hang on.</p>
      <p class="fine">Built for revenue organizations with 50 sellers or more. Below that scale, ask Bruce about the Value Edge on its own.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-bone2">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The three hours</p>
      <h2>What your team walks out with</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        {EDGES.map((e) => (
          <div class="card">
            <p class="eyebrow">{e.num} &nbsp;{e.name}</p>
            <h3>{e.promise}</h3>
            <p>{e.blurb}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-ink band-measure">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How to start</p>
      <h2>Talk to whichever of us you know.</h2>
      {/* No form and no shared inbox, on purpose. The three contract with
           clients individually, so a single lead form would need an owner and
           a routing rule that does not exist. An inquiry goes to a person.
           Whoever gets the mail loops in the other two. */}
      <p>Write to us or give us a call. Reach whichever of us you already know, or whoever owns the edge you most need. We will loop in the other two.</p>

      <div class="contacts">
        {FACULTY.map((p) => (
          <div class="contact">
            {p.photo && <img src={p.photo} alt="" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" aria-hidden="true" />}
            <b>{p.name}</b>
            <span>{p.edge}</span>
            <a class="btn" href={inquiryLink(p)}>Email {p.name.split(' ')[0]}</a>
            <a class="contact-mail" href={inquiryLink(p)}>{p.email}</a>
            <a class="contact-tel" href={`tel:${p.phone}`}>{p.phoneDisplay}</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="cta-pair">
        <a class="more" href="/#dates">Or come to a public session first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
